    "html_url": "https://github.com/romaine-life/kill-me/commit/e77b3ac1c45154be4384919ac5a1d5b44787a5fc",
    "message": "Make a logged soreness day clickable wherever it is drawn\n\nThe journal list had the only way into the editor — a wrench icon beside the\ndate. Lanes and Timeline draw the same entries and offered hover detail only,\nso the view you spot a mistake in was not the view you could fix it in. Since\nLanes is now the landing view, the default page had no edit affordance at all.\n\nA soreness entry is identified by (date, sourceWorkoutId), and both views\nalready hold that pair for every cell they draw, so each can hand off to the\neditor the wrench opens: a lane stripe's logged day, and a filled cell in a\nrecovery curve. Unlogged days stay inert — there is no entry to edit.",
