    "event": "committed",
    "html_url": "https://github.com/romaine-life/kill-me/commit/0f57786fad45e8715568b35dee57346e905a45da",
    "message": "Give kill-me its own devctl environment\n\ndevctl will not mark an environment ready until the process on the port proves\nit is the exact instance, project, worktree and revision it was asked for, and\nkill-me could satisfy neither half of that: no identity endpoint, and Vite's\ndefault host resolves verbatim to ::1 alone here while the probe and the Caddy\nroute in front of it both dial 127.0.0.1. Every attempt to run this repo under\ndevctl therefore ended as a failed launch that left an orphaned Vite behind.\n\nSo serve /__devctl/health off the DEVCTL_* environment, bind IPv4 loopback, and\nhonour the assigned port. The endpoint is serve-only and inert unless devctl\nlaunched us, so it cannot reach a production build.\n\nBinding 127.0.0.1 has one consequence worth writing down: headless Chrome does\nnot fall back from ::1, so a screenshot against localhost now fails silently\nwith no PNG at all. The verification recipe uses the literal address.",
